{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014QX2sDgCD5HWCQNW75B3wM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ELSA Speak phoneme-level pronunciation feedback proprietary speech recognition technology\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"7 Best ELSA Speak Alternatives for Professionals (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://www.talaera.com/business-english-platforms/elsa-speak-alternatives/\"},{\"title\":\"ELSA Speak Review 2026: AI English Pronunciation Coach\",\"url\":\"https://www.buildfastwithai.com/ai-tools/elsa-speak\"},{\"title\":\"ELSA | API\",\"url\":\"https://elsaspeak.com/en/elsa-api/\"},{\"title\":\"ELSA Speak Review: Can It Perfect Your Pronunciation? | by Emma Miller | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@emmamillerw1990/elsa-speak-review-can-it-perfect-your-pronunciation-8c737d8ffdd1\"},{\"title\":\"How does ELSA’s pronunciation feedback work? - ELSA Speak FAQs\",\"url\":\"https://elsaspeak.com/en/faqs/how-does-elsas-pronunciation-feedback-work\"},{\"title\":\"Machine learning applications in speech recognition and language learning: | by Ngan P | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://nganp.medium.com/machine-learning-applications-in-speech-recognition-and-language-learning-1416fcae760b\"},{\"title\":\"ELSA | Speech Analyzer. Instant, personalized feedback on your speech\",\"url\":\"https://speechanalyzer.elsaspeak.com/\"},{\"title\":\"ELSA Speak Review: Is It Worth It for Pronunciation? - Study English at 3D ACADEMY, a Language School in Cebu, Philippines\",\"url\":\"https://3d-universal.com/en/blogs/elsa-speak-review.html\"},{\"title\":\"Leading English Language Pronunciation App ELSA Provides Free Access For Students\",\"url\":\"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20200408005066/en/Leading-English-Language-Pronunciation-App-ELSA-Provides-Free-Access-For-Students\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about ELSA Speak's phoneme-level pronunciation feedback and proprietary speech recognition technology:\n\n## Phoneme-Level Pronunciation Feedback\n\nELSA delivers phoneme-level pronunciation scoring with AI-powered instant feedback that catches subtle errors most human listeners would miss. It uses advanced speech recognition to analyze spoken English down to individual phonemes (sound units), comparing them to native speaker reference standards and providing guidance on tongue and lip placement.\n\n## Proprietary Speech Recognition Technology\n\nELSA uses proprietary speech technology with deep learning and AI to detect people's pronunciation mistakes with 95%+ accuracy. ELSA's core architecture is its proprietary ML algorithm that analyses patterns of speech features extracted down to the phoneme level.\n\n## How It Works\n\nELSA Speak uses advanced speech recognition and AI technology to analyze your pronunciation and provide detailed feedback on sounds, stress, and intonation. ELSA Speak listens to the way language learners pronounce words, sentences or conversations to pinpoint exact errors and provide real-time feedback on pronunciation mistakes with specific suggestions on how to improve.\n\nFounded in 2015 by Stanford alum Vu Van and Dr. Xavier Anguera, a veteran in speech recognition and AI, ELSA is a Silicon Valley-based company that uses proprietary speech recognition technology and artificial intelligence to help language learners improve their English pronunciation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e45f550-5a65-4305-802e-931b3b49c5e2","uuid":"4ef4ca70-c483-40fb-87e7-979ba5f62e68","timestamp":"2026-08-11T02:33:04.497Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ELSA Speak phoneme-level pronunciation feedback proprietary speech recognition technology","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01FBysT8nwwZsX2vf58VXu45","content":[{"title":"7 Best ELSA Speak Alternatives for Professionals (2026)","url":"https://www.talaera.com/business-english-platforms/elsa-speak-alternatives/"},{"title":"ELSA Speak Review 2026: AI English Pronunciation Coach","url":"https://www.buildfastwithai.com/ai-tools/elsa-speak"},{"title":"ELSA | API","url":"https://elsaspeak.com/en/elsa-api/"},{"title":"ELSA Speak Review: Can It Perfect Your Pronunciation? | by Emma Miller | Medium","url":"https://medium.com/@emmamillerw1990/elsa-speak-review-can-it-perfect-your-pronunciation-8c737d8ffdd1"},{"title":"How does ELSA’s pronunciation feedback work? - ELSA Speak FAQs","url":"https://elsaspeak.com/en/faqs/how-does-elsas-pronunciation-feedback-work"},{"title":"Machine learning applications in speech recognition and language learning: | by Ngan P | Medium","url":"https://nganp.medium.com/machine-learning-applications-in-speech-recognition-and-language-learning-1416fcae760b"},{"title":"ELSA | Speech Analyzer. Instant, personalized feedback on your speech","url":"https://speechanalyzer.elsaspeak.com/"},{"title":"ELSA Speak Review: Is It Worth It for Pronunciation? - Study English at 3D ACADEMY, a Language School in Cebu, Philippines","url":"https://3d-universal.com/en/blogs/elsa-speak-review.html"},{"title":"Leading English Language Pronunciation App ELSA Provides Free Access For Students","url":"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20200408005066/en/Leading-English-Language-Pronunciation-App-ELSA-Provides-Free-Access-For-Students"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about ELSA Speak's phoneme-level pronunciation feedback and proprietary speech recognition technology:\n\n## Phoneme-Level Pronunciation Feedback\n\nELSA delivers phoneme-level pronunciation scoring with AI-powered instant feedback that catches subtle errors most human listeners would miss. It uses advanced speech recognition to analyze spoken English down to individual phonemes (sound units), comparing them to native speaker reference standards and providing guidance on tongue and lip placement.\n\n## Proprietary Speech Recognition Technology\n\nELSA uses proprietary speech technology with deep learning and AI to detect people's pronunciation mistakes with 95%+ accuracy. ELSA's core architecture is its proprietary ML algorithm that analyses patterns of speech features extracted down to the phoneme level.\n\n## How It Works\n\nELSA Speak uses advanced speech recognition and AI technology to analyze your pronunciation and provide detailed feedback on sounds, stress, and intonation. ELSA Speak listens to the way language learners pronounce words, sentences or conversations to pinpoint exact errors and provide real-time feedback on pronunciation mistakes with specific suggestions on how to improve.\n\nFounded in 2015 by Stanford alum Vu Van and Dr. Xavier Anguera, a veteran in speech recognition and AI, ELSA is a Silicon Valley-based company that uses proprietary speech recognition technology and artificial intelligence to help language learners improve their English pronunciation."],"durationSeconds":6.467504375000004,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TseAD3m3yhtLVha5V6zFTR","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Duolingo Birdbrain how it works exercise difficulty prediction model blog\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Unveiling the AI Powering Duolingo\",\"url\":\"https://www.toolify.ai/gpts/unveiling-the-ai-powering-duolingo-111301\"},{\"title\":\"How Duolingo Predicts When You’ll Forget Using Data Mining | by Rohith R | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@rohithparambil/how-duolingo-predicts-when-youll-forget-using-data-mining-2abab0a921f4\"},{\"title\":\"AI-Driven Learning Personalization: How Duolingo Revolutionized Language Education with Machine Learning – Millennial Partners\",\"url\":\"https://millennial.ae/ai-driven-learning-personalization-how-duolingo-revolutionized-language-education-with-machine-learning/\"},{\"title\":\"Uncovering the AI Behind Duolingo: Birdbrain, the Personalization Powerhouse — TOM DACCORD\",\"url\":\"https://www.tomdaccord.com/blog/ai-and-duolingo\"},{\"title\":\"AI at Duolingo: Transforming Language Learning\",\"url\":\"https://angelinepoitout.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/AI-at-Duolingo-Transforming-Language-Learning-1-1.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Duolingo AI Personalization: How Birdbrain Works\",\"url\":\"https://www.buildmvpfast.com/blog/ai-learning-personalization-duolingo-ai-driven-lessons-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Second Language Acquisition Modeling: An Ensemble Approach\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1806.04525\"},{\"title\":\"Accurate Predictions in Education with Discrete Variational Inference\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.23484\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Duolingo's Birdbrain and how it works:\n\n## Overview\n\nDuolingo's R&D and AI teams — in collaboration with Carnegie Mellon University — designed an adaptive learning architecture called the Birdbrain Model, a deep learning system trained to predict how likely a learner is to answer each exercise correctly.\n\n## How It Works\n\nBirdbrain is an AI system that estimates the difficulty of a particular exercise and the proficiency of the user, and based on learner responses, it uses an algorithm to instantly select new exercises for the next lesson.\n\nBirdbrain estimates the difficulty of each exercise by calculating the difficulty of its various components and when a learner gets an exercise wrong, Birdbrain lowers the estimate of the user's ability and raises the estimate of the exercise's difficulty.\n\n## The \"Goldilocks Zone\"\n\nThe platform aims for learners to answer around 80 percent of questions correctly. This level of difficulty is challenging enough to sustain engagement, but not so difficult as to become discouraging, occupying the so-called Goldilocks zone of learning.\n\n## Performance\n\nAfter about 100 exercises (roughly 5-6 lessons), the system has enough data to start generating fully personalized sequences. Before that, you're on a default curriculum. Most users don't even notice the switch because the transition is gradual, but the accuracy of Birdbrain's predictions jumps noticeably after that threshold.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e45f550-5a65-4305-802e-931b3b49c5e2","uuid":"ba9020f2-2c68-4073-a744-cbc3e6febfbf","timestamp":"2026-08-11T02:33:04.731Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Duolingo Birdbrain how it works exercise difficulty prediction model blog","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01WAG1yx7JPep82cVcUkGAFu","content":[{"title":"Unveiling the AI Powering Duolingo","url":"https://www.toolify.ai/gpts/unveiling-the-ai-powering-duolingo-111301"},{"title":"How Duolingo Predicts When You’ll Forget Using Data Mining | by Rohith R | Medium","url":"https://medium.com/@rohithparambil/how-duolingo-predicts-when-youll-forget-using-data-mining-2abab0a921f4"},{"title":"AI-Driven Learning Personalization: How Duolingo Revolutionized Language Education with Machine Learning – Millennial Partners","url":"https://millennial.ae/ai-driven-learning-personalization-how-duolingo-revolutionized-language-education-with-machine-learning/"},{"title":"Uncovering the AI Behind Duolingo: Birdbrain, the Personalization Powerhouse — TOM DACCORD","url":"https://www.tomdaccord.com/blog/ai-and-duolingo"},{"title":"AI at Duolingo: Transforming Language Learning","url":"https://angelinepoitout.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/AI-at-Duolingo-Transforming-Language-Learning-1-1.pdf"},{"title":"Duolingo AI Personalization: How Birdbrain Works","url":"https://www.buildmvpfast.com/blog/ai-learning-personalization-duolingo-ai-driven-lessons-2026"},{"title":"Second Language Acquisition Modeling: An Ensemble Approach","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1806.04525"},{"title":"Accurate Predictions in Education with Discrete Variational Inference","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.23484"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about Duolingo's Birdbrain and how it works:\n\n## Overview\n\nDuolingo's R&D and AI teams — in collaboration with Carnegie Mellon University — designed an adaptive learning architecture called the Birdbrain Model, a deep learning system trained to predict how likely a learner is to answer each exercise correctly.\n\n## How It Works\n\nBirdbrain is an AI system that estimates the difficulty of a particular exercise and the proficiency of the user, and based on learner responses, it uses an algorithm to instantly select new exercises for the next lesson.\n\nBirdbrain estimates the difficulty of each exercise by calculating the difficulty of its various components and when a learner gets an exercise wrong, Birdbrain lowers the estimate of the user's ability and raises the estimate of the exercise's difficulty.\n\n## The \"Goldilocks Zone\"\n\nThe platform aims for learners to answer around 80 percent of questions correctly. This level of difficulty is challenging enough to sustain engagement, but not so difficult as to become discouraging, occupying the so-called Goldilocks zone of learning.\n\n## Performance\n\nAfter about 100 exercises (roughly 5-6 lessons), the system has enough data to start generating fully personalized sequences. Before that, you're on a default curriculum. Most users don't even notice the switch because the transition is gradual, but the accuracy of Birdbrain's predictions jumps noticeably after that threshold."],"durationSeconds":7.309019667,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LjL1VXGNw8aXMhevVH6YAw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Duolingo half-life regression spaced repetition Settles Meeder paper\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Analysis of Half-life Regression Model Made by Duolingo\",\"url\":\"https://papousek.github.io/analysis-of-half-life-regression-model-made-by-duolingo.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - duolingo/halflife-regression · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/duolingo/halflife-regression\"},{\"title\":\"halflife-regression/experiment.py at master · duolingo/halflife-regression\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/duolingo/halflife-regression/blob/master/experiment.py\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive Forgetting Curves for Spaced Repetition Language Learning - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7334729/\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] A Trainable Spaced Repetition Model for Language Learning | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/A-Trainable-Spaced-Repetition-Model-for-Language-Settles-Meeder/cb836d2b8e126dc31ded5e674d73021604dcc6e0\"},{\"title\":\"A Trainable Spaced Repetition Model for Language Learning\",\"url\":\"https://research.duolingo.com/papers/settles.acl16.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A Trainable Spaced Repetition Model for Language Learning\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/anthology-files/pdf/P/P16/P16-1174.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Research - Duolingo\",\"url\":\"https://research.duolingo.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Using Simpson's Paradox to Discover Interesting Patterns in Behavioral   Data\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1805.03094\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive Forgetting Curves for Spaced Repetition Language Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2004.11327\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive information about the Settles and Meeder paper on Duolingo's half-life regression model. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Paper Overview\n\nBurr Settles (from Duolingo) and Brendan Meeder proposed a model predicting the probability of recall during practice with Duolingo based on the lag time since a particular item was last presented by a learner. The original paper is called \"A Trainable Spaced Repetition Model for Language Learning\" and was published in 2016 in the Proceedings of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL), pages 1848-1858.\n\n## Model Description\n\nHalf-life regression (HLR) is a model for spaced repetition practice with particular applications to second language acquisition, which marries psycholinguistic theory with modern machine learning techniques, indirectly estimating the \"half-life\" of words (and potentially any other item or fact) in a student's long-term memory.\n\n## Results\n\nUsing data from Duolingo, HLR models reduced error by 45%+ compared to several baselines at predicting student recall rates.\n\n## Data and Implementation\n\nThe data used to develop their half-life regression spaced repetition algorithm is a collection of 13 million user-word pairs for learners of several languages with a variety of language backgrounds, including practice recall rates, lag times between practices, and other morpho-lexical metadata. The repository contains a public release of the data and code used for experiments in the paper.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e45f550-5a65-4305-802e-931b3b49c5e2","uuid":"809e190e-7465-43f0-9a82-a12d269cf8cf","timestamp":"2026-08-11T02:33:05.384Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Duolingo half-life regression spaced repetition Settles Meeder paper","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Mj4f65uN7zALvk4Crtp4mV","content":[{"title":"Analysis of Half-life Regression Model Made by Duolingo","url":"https://papousek.github.io/analysis-of-half-life-regression-model-made-by-duolingo.html"},{"title":"GitHub - duolingo/halflife-regression · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/duolingo/halflife-regression"},{"title":"halflife-regression/experiment.py at master · duolingo/halflife-regression","url":"https://github.com/duolingo/halflife-regression/blob/master/experiment.py"},{"title":"Adaptive Forgetting Curves for Spaced Repetition Language Learning - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7334729/"},{"title":"[PDF] A Trainable Spaced Repetition Model for Language Learning | Semantic Scholar","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/A-Trainable-Spaced-Repetition-Model-for-Language-Settles-Meeder/cb836d2b8e126dc31ded5e674d73021604dcc6e0"},{"title":"A Trainable Spaced Repetition Model for Language Learning","url":"https://research.duolingo.com/papers/settles.acl16.pdf"},{"title":"A Trainable Spaced Repetition Model for Language Learning","url":"https://aclanthology.org/anthology-files/pdf/P/P16/P16-1174.pdf"},{"title":"Research - Duolingo","url":"https://research.duolingo.com/"},{"title":"Using Simpson's Paradox to Discover Interesting Patterns in Behavioral   Data","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1805.03094"},{"title":"Adaptive Forgetting Curves for Spaced Repetition Language Learning","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2004.11327"}]},"I found comprehensive information about the Settles and Meeder paper on Duolingo's half-life regression model. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Paper Overview\n\nBurr Settles (from Duolingo) and Brendan Meeder proposed a model predicting the probability of recall during practice with Duolingo based on the lag time since a particular item was last presented by a learner. The original paper is called \"A Trainable Spaced Repetition Model for Language Learning\" and was published in 2016 in the Proceedings of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL), pages 1848-1858.\n\n## Model Description\n\nHalf-life regression (HLR) is a model for spaced repetition practice with particular applications to second language acquisition, which marries psycholinguistic theory with modern machine learning techniques, indirectly estimating the \"half-life\" of words (and potentially any other item or fact) in a student's long-term memory.\n\n## Results\n\nUsing data from Duolingo, HLR models reduced error by 45%+ compared to several baselines at predicting student recall rates.\n\n## Data and Implementation\n\nThe data used to develop their half-life regression spaced repetition algorithm is a collection of 13 million user-word pairs for learners of several languages with a variety of language backgrounds, including practice recall rates, lag times between practices, and other morpho-lexical metadata. The repository contains a public release of the data and code used for experiments in the paper."],"durationSeconds":7.875506207999992,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011rebTkUqBWEk3B2XdAPUFB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Speak app AI tutor mechanism speech recognition roleplay lesson feedback OpenAI\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Speak Explained: The OpenAI-Backed Language App (2026) - Beginners in AI\",\"url\":\"https://beginnersinai.org/speak-explained/\"},{\"title\":\"Speak - The language learning app that gets you speaking\",\"url\":\"https://www.speak.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Speak App Review 2026: Is This AI English Tutor Worth It\",\"url\":\"https://learn.kotoenglish.com/blog/speak-app-review/\"},{\"title\":\"Speak Review: AI Language Tutor for Speaking Practice\",\"url\":\"https://tooldirectory.ai/tools/speak\"},{\"title\":\"Speak App Review: Is It Worth It in 2026?\",\"url\":\"https://languatalk.com/blog/speak-app-review/\"},{\"title\":\"Live Roleplays powered by OpenAI Realtime API\",\"url\":\"https://www.speak.com/blog/live-roleplays\"},{\"title\":\"Speak Review 2026 - AI Language Tutor\",\"url\":\"https://tooliverse.ai/tools/speak\"},{\"title\":\"Speak App Review 2026: Is It Worth $18 a Month?\",\"url\":\"https://speakshark.com/blog/speak-app-review-2026\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the Speak app's AI tutor mechanism:\n\n## Core Technology and Speech Recognition\n\nSpeak uses OpenAI's Realtime API (the same low-latency voice infrastructure behind ChatGPT Voice) for the conversation engine, combined with Speak's own curriculum and feedback systems trained on language-learning data. With the Realtime API on GPT-4o, their AI tutor responds as fast or faster than a human partner would, and can understand and provide feedback on aspects of speech beyond the pure text transcript, like tone, pronunciation, prosody, and more.\n\n## The Learning Framework\n\nSpeak uses a proprietary three-step framework called the Speak Method: 1) Learn — Each lesson teaches you the phrases and patterns that native speakers actually use in real situations. 2) Practice — You repeat those patterns across different situations until they become automatic. 3) Apply — You use what you've learned in a real back-and-forth conversation with the Speak Tutor AI, which gives you feedback on what actually matters.\n\n## Roleplay and Feedback\n\nThe app includes scripted real-world scenarios like ordering coffee, job interview practice, asking for directions, and negotiating a price with AI characters, and after each roleplay you get specific feedback on accuracy and use of varied language.\n\n## AI Tutor Capabilities\n\nThe AI tutor offers open-ended conversation on any topic, where you set a topic, the AI talks with you in the target language, corrects when needed, and adapts to your level.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e45f550-5a65-4305-802e-931b3b49c5e2","uuid":"e9f63241-58a5-4132-989d-e09e03a6f345","timestamp":"2026-08-11T02:33:06.246Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Speak app AI tutor mechanism speech recognition roleplay lesson feedback OpenAI","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01YDWCRJTuCGXJVbTN8VbXKu","content":[{"title":"Speak Explained: The OpenAI-Backed Language App (2026) - Beginners in AI","url":"https://beginnersinai.org/speak-explained/"},{"title":"Speak - The language learning app that gets you speaking","url":"https://www.speak.com/"},{"title":"Speak App Review 2026: Is This AI English Tutor Worth It","url":"https://learn.kotoenglish.com/blog/speak-app-review/"},{"title":"Speak Review: AI Language Tutor for Speaking Practice","url":"https://tooldirectory.ai/tools/speak"},{"title":"Speak App Review: Is It Worth It in 2026?","url":"https://languatalk.com/blog/speak-app-review/"},{"title":"Live Roleplays powered by OpenAI Realtime API","url":"https://www.speak.com/blog/live-roleplays"},{"title":"Speak Review 2026 - AI Language Tutor","url":"https://tooliverse.ai/tools/speak"},{"title":"Speak App Review 2026: Is It Worth $18 a Month?","url":"https://speakshark.com/blog/speak-app-review-2026"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the Speak app's AI tutor mechanism:\n\n## Core Technology and Speech Recognition\n\nSpeak uses OpenAI's Realtime API (the same low-latency voice infrastructure behind ChatGPT Voice) for the conversation engine, combined with Speak's own curriculum and feedback systems trained on language-learning data. With the Realtime API on GPT-4o, their AI tutor responds as fast or faster than a human partner would, and can understand and provide feedback on aspects of speech beyond the pure text transcript, like tone, pronunciation, prosody, and more.\n\n## The Learning Framework\n\nSpeak uses a proprietary three-step framework called the Speak Method: 1) Learn — Each lesson teaches you the phrases and patterns that native speakers actually use in real situations. 2) Practice — You repeat those patterns across different situations until they become automatic. 3) Apply — You use what you've learned in a real back-and-forth conversation with the Speak Tutor AI, which gives you feedback on what actually matters.\n\n## Roleplay and Feedback\n\nThe app includes scripted real-world scenarios like ordering coffee, job interview practice, asking for directions, and negotiating a price with AI characters, and after each roleplay you get specific feedback on accuracy and use of varied language.\n\n## AI Tutor Capabilities\n\nThe AI tutor offers open-ended conversation on any topic, where you set a topic, the AI talks with you in the target language, corrects when needed, and adapts to your level."],"durationSeconds":7.735712667,"searchCount":1}}
