{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SuGnmG84kkp53BkoxeveGG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Shadow Health digital clinical experience conversation engine virtual patient scoring mechanism\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Digital Clinical Experiences™ | Shadow Health®\",\"url\":\"https://www.elsevier.com/products/shadow-health\"},{\"title\":\"Shadow Health Digital Clinical Experience Orientation: A Comprehensive Guide To Virtual Nursing Success - Unitaid\",\"url\":\"https://www.unitaid.eu/health-digital-clinical-experience-orientation-5i2a.html\"},{\"title\":\"Elsevier acquires Healthcare Simulation Company Shadow Health | HealthySimulation.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.healthysimulation.com/elsevier-acquires-shadow-health/\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding Shadow Health: A Guide for Nursing Students (2025)\",\"url\":\"https://academicresearchbureau.com/shadow-healt/\"},{\"title\":\"Shadow Health | Virtual Nursing Simulation | Complete Guide\",\"url\":\"https://academicresearchbureau.com/shadow-he/\"},{\"title\":\"Shadow Health® (2026) – NHE Faculty Training\",\"url\":\"https://elsevierresources.com/nhe-faculty-training/shadow-health/\"},{\"title\":\"Shadow Health – NHE Student Training\",\"url\":\"https://elsevierresources.com/nhe-student-training/shadow-health/\"},{\"title\":\"Nursing Simulation for Nursing students | Shadow Health\",\"url\":\"http://shadowfithealth.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Shadow Health Assessment Help by Experts | Nurse My Grade\",\"url\":\"https://nursemygrade.com/shadow-health-help-online\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's comprehensive information about Shadow Health's digital clinical experience, conversation engine, and virtual patient scoring:\n\n## Overview\n\nShadow Health Digital Clinical Experiences™ (DCE) offers high-fidelity, screen-based simulations to help nursing students build patient care skills through realistic virtual patient encounters, and features 80+ life-like, diverse Digital Standardized Patients™ who can answer millions of unique questions using a patented Conversation Engine.\n\n## Conversation Engine\n\nThe patented Conversation Engine allows students to use their own words to communicate, and allows students to type or speak naturally — as they would in a real clinical encounter — rather than selecting from pre-programmed drop-down menus. This free-text interaction model is what sets Shadow Health apart from earlier generations of simulation software, making the learning experience far more authentic and transferable to real-world nursing practice.\n\n## Virtual Patient Interactions\n\nStudents engage with Digital Standardized Patients™ using a state-of-the-art conversation engine and interactive 3D imagery to perform assessments, practice documentation, and demonstrate critical thinking.\n\n## Scoring and Performance Assessment\n\nThe orientation introduces the DCE Score, a metric that evaluates your performance based on national standards, focusing on data collection and documentation. Instant feedback helps learners understand their performance and clinical reasoning accuracy.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e45f550-5a65-4305-802e-931b3b49c5e2","uuid":"14723ead-f0d7-49b5-b073-9099eefb5e85","timestamp":"2026-08-11T02:33:31.847Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Shadow Health digital clinical experience conversation engine virtual patient scoring mechanism","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_017FvtcXMAM8kZiMxHLvUswy","content":[{"title":"Digital Clinical Experiences™ | Shadow Health®","url":"https://www.elsevier.com/products/shadow-health"},{"title":"Shadow Health Digital Clinical Experience Orientation: A Comprehensive Guide To Virtual Nursing Success - Unitaid","url":"https://www.unitaid.eu/health-digital-clinical-experience-orientation-5i2a.html"},{"title":"Elsevier acquires Healthcare Simulation Company Shadow Health | HealthySimulation.com","url":"https://www.healthysimulation.com/elsevier-acquires-shadow-health/"},{"title":"Understanding Shadow Health: A Guide for Nursing Students (2025)","url":"https://academicresearchbureau.com/shadow-healt/"},{"title":"Shadow Health | Virtual Nursing Simulation | Complete Guide","url":"https://academicresearchbureau.com/shadow-he/"},{"title":"Shadow Health® (2026) – NHE Faculty Training","url":"https://elsevierresources.com/nhe-faculty-training/shadow-health/"},{"title":"Shadow Health – NHE Student Training","url":"https://elsevierresources.com/nhe-student-training/shadow-health/"},{"title":"Nursing Simulation for Nursing students | Shadow Health","url":"http://shadowfithealth.com/"},{"title":"Shadow Health Assessment Help by Experts | Nurse My Grade","url":"https://nursemygrade.com/shadow-health-help-online"}]},"Based on the search results, here's comprehensive information about Shadow Health's digital clinical experience, conversation engine, and virtual patient scoring:\n\n## Overview\n\nShadow Health Digital Clinical Experiences™ (DCE) offers high-fidelity, screen-based simulations to help nursing students build patient care skills through realistic virtual patient encounters, and features 80+ life-like, diverse Digital Standardized Patients™ who can answer millions of unique questions using a patented Conversation Engine.\n\n## Conversation Engine\n\nThe patented Conversation Engine allows students to use their own words to communicate, and allows students to type or speak naturally — as they would in a real clinical encounter — rather than selecting from pre-programmed drop-down menus. This free-text interaction model is what sets Shadow Health apart from earlier generations of simulation software, making the learning experience far more authentic and transferable to real-world nursing practice.\n\n## Virtual Patient Interactions\n\nStudents engage with Digital Standardized Patients™ using a state-of-the-art conversation engine and interactive 3D imagery to perform assessments, practice documentation, and demonstrate critical thinking.\n\n## Scoring and Performance Assessment\n\nThe orientation introduces the DCE Score, a metric that evaluates your performance based on national standards, focusing on data collection and documentation. Instant feedback helps learners understand their performance and clinical reasoning accuracy."],"durationSeconds":6.9848130419999945,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019GR8428DqqrcWc6yaiBeYM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Exercism representers analyzers automated feedback normalized representation docs\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Representers | Exercism's Docs\",\"url\":\"https://exercism.org/docs/building/product/representers\"},{\"title\":\"Analyzers, Representers & Syllabuses - What's new in Exercism?\",\"url\":\"https://exercism.org/blog/whats-new-in-v3-with-angelika\"},{\"title\":\"Build Representer and Analyzer · Issue #13 · exercism/solidity\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/exercism/solidity/issues/13\"},{\"title\":\"docs/building/tooling/representers/README.md at main · exercism/docs\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/exercism/docs/blob/main/building/tooling/representers/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Build Representer and Analyzer · Issue #277 · exercism/lua\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/exercism/lua/issues/277\"},{\"title\":\"How to give feedback on representations | Exercism's Docs\",\"url\":\"https://exercism.org/docs/mentoring/how-to-give-feedback-on-representations\"},{\"title\":\"Introducing Representers\",\"url\":\"https://exercism.org/blog/introducing-representers\"},{\"title\":\"exercism-v3/docs/features-of-v3.md at master · workingjubilee/exercism-v3\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/workingjubilee/exercism-v3/blob/master/docs/features-of-v3.md\"},{\"title\":\"v3/docs/features-of-v3.md at main · exercism/v3\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/exercism/v3/blob/main/docs/features-of-v3.md\"},{\"title\":\"Build representer · Issue #678 · exercism/c\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/exercism/c/issues/678\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Exercism's representers and analyzers for automated feedback:\n\n## Representers\n\nA representer is a piece of software that takes a student's solution and returns a normalized representation of it, which is then used to streamline automated feedback and classification. It normalizes formatting, removes comments and documentation, and replaces function and variable names with placeholders.\n\nA representation is an extraction of a solution to its essence with normalized names, comments, spacing, etc., but still uniquely identifying the approach taken. This dramatically reduces the amount of duplicate mentoring that needs to happen.\n\n## Analyzers\n\nIn Exercism v3, there are two types of tools for automated feedback: Analyzers and Representers, with the Analyzer being a tool that looks for specific characteristics in a solution and returns to the student a list of predefined comments about what it finds. Analyzers automatically assess student's submissions and provide mentor-style commentary, and can be used to catch common mistakes and/or do complex solution analysis that can't easily be done directly in a test suite.\n\n## How They Work Together\n\nFor each unique representation, a mentor can leave feedback on that representation, and that feedback will be presented to every student that submits a similar solution that has the same representation.\n\nEach track maintains its own representer, specific to that language.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e45f550-5a65-4305-802e-931b3b49c5e2","uuid":"fdbd276f-54a8-424f-8c36-735e48070186","timestamp":"2026-08-11T02:33:32.191Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Exercism representers analyzers automated feedback normalized representation docs","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01QV7zwREqjf3XmA6KtogmFd","content":[{"title":"Representers | Exercism's Docs","url":"https://exercism.org/docs/building/product/representers"},{"title":"Analyzers, Representers & Syllabuses - What's new in Exercism?","url":"https://exercism.org/blog/whats-new-in-v3-with-angelika"},{"title":"Build Representer and Analyzer · Issue #13 · exercism/solidity","url":"https://github.com/exercism/solidity/issues/13"},{"title":"docs/building/tooling/representers/README.md at main · exercism/docs","url":"https://github.com/exercism/docs/blob/main/building/tooling/representers/README.md"},{"title":"Build Representer and Analyzer · Issue #277 · exercism/lua","url":"https://github.com/exercism/lua/issues/277"},{"title":"How to give feedback on representations | Exercism's Docs","url":"https://exercism.org/docs/mentoring/how-to-give-feedback-on-representations"},{"title":"Introducing Representers","url":"https://exercism.org/blog/introducing-representers"},{"title":"exercism-v3/docs/features-of-v3.md at master · workingjubilee/exercism-v3","url":"https://github.com/workingjubilee/exercism-v3/blob/master/docs/features-of-v3.md"},{"title":"v3/docs/features-of-v3.md at main · exercism/v3","url":"https://github.com/exercism/v3/blob/main/docs/features-of-v3.md"},{"title":"Build representer · Issue #678 · exercism/c","url":"https://github.com/exercism/c/issues/678"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about Exercism's representers and analyzers for automated feedback:\n\n## Representers\n\nA representer is a piece of software that takes a student's solution and returns a normalized representation of it, which is then used to streamline automated feedback and classification. It normalizes formatting, removes comments and documentation, and replaces function and variable names with placeholders.\n\nA representation is an extraction of a solution to its essence with normalized names, comments, spacing, etc., but still uniquely identifying the approach taken. This dramatically reduces the amount of duplicate mentoring that needs to happen.\n\n## Analyzers\n\nIn Exercism v3, there are two types of tools for automated feedback: Analyzers and Representers, with the Analyzer being a tool that looks for specific characteristics in a solution and returns to the student a list of predefined comments about what it finds. Analyzers automatically assess student's submissions and provide mentor-style commentary, and can be used to catch common mistakes and/or do complex solution analysis that can't easily be done directly in a test suite.\n\n## How They Work Together\n\nFor each unique representation, a mentor can leave feedback on that representation, and that feedback will be presented to every student that submits a similar solution that has the same representation.\n\nEach track maintains its own representer, specific to that language."],"durationSeconds":7.318389958,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Erxvqh7QubQCY4HgxhGcsS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Boot.dev Boots AI mentor socratic hints no answers mechanism\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Boot.dev: Gamified Backend Development Courses\",\"url\":\"https://tooldirectory.ai/tools/boot-dev\"},{\"title\":\"The Boot.dev Beat. October 2023 | Boot.dev\",\"url\":\"https://www.boot.dev/blog/news/bootdev-beat-2023-10/\"},{\"title\":\"About | Boot.dev\",\"url\":\"https://www.boot.dev/about\"},{\"title\":\"Boots, a Wizard Bear That Codes | Boot.dev\",\"url\":\"https://blog.boot.dev/wiki/boots/\"},{\"title\":\"Learn Python for Beginners: Boots | Boot.dev\",\"url\":\"https://www.boot.dev/lessons/e4fac74c-9d67-41ad-a85c-c579cb3ad76f\"},{\"title\":\"Boots, a Wizard Bear that Codes | Boot.dev\",\"url\":\"https://boot.dev/blog/news/introducing-boots-ai-code-explainer\"},{\"title\":\"When Learning to Code Feels Like an RPG: My Boot.dev Review — Class Central\",\"url\":\"https://www.classcentral.com/report/review-boot-dev/\"},{\"title\":\"Introducing Boots, the Artificially Intelligent Bear That Explains Code | Boot.dev\",\"url\":\"https://blog.boot.dev/news/introducing-boots-ai-code-explainer/\"},{\"title\":\"Learn to Code | Boot.dev\",\"url\":\"https://www.boot.dev/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Boot.dev's Boots AI mentor and its Socratic method:\n\n## Boots: The Socratic AI Mentor\n\nBoot.dev's built-in AI mentor — Boots answers questions about the lesson you are on Socratically, with hints instead of solutions.\n\n### How It Works\n\nBoots has been instructed to use the Socratic method to help you learn, which means he'll ask you questions to help you learn rather than give you the answer. Boots is an AI chatbot (like ChatGPT) that has access to your lesson.\n\n### The Penalty Mechanism\n\nTo encourage independent problem-solving, Boot.dev has implemented an incentive system: Starting a conversation with Boots before you've completed a lesson costs 1 baked salmon (he's a hungry guy), or, if you don't have one, 50% of the XP for the lesson. However, chatting with Boots after you've completed a lesson is free, and encouraged for deepening your understanding.\n\n### Philosophy Behind the Design\n\nBoots is designed to not give you the answer, but instead use the Socratic method to help you figure it out yourself, and you're actually penalized (in game terms) for using him so you'll only use him when you truly need the help.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e45f550-5a65-4305-802e-931b3b49c5e2","uuid":"65f8f12e-5cbc-4eb8-a73c-aaaf0d67e6e5","timestamp":"2026-08-11T02:33:32.310Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Boot.dev Boots AI mentor socratic hints no answers mechanism","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01E8YS5wLVEzktLarwn8Rz6G","content":[{"title":"Boot.dev: Gamified Backend Development Courses","url":"https://tooldirectory.ai/tools/boot-dev"},{"title":"The Boot.dev Beat. October 2023 | Boot.dev","url":"https://www.boot.dev/blog/news/bootdev-beat-2023-10/"},{"title":"About | Boot.dev","url":"https://www.boot.dev/about"},{"title":"Boots, a Wizard Bear That Codes | Boot.dev","url":"https://blog.boot.dev/wiki/boots/"},{"title":"Learn Python for Beginners: Boots | Boot.dev","url":"https://www.boot.dev/lessons/e4fac74c-9d67-41ad-a85c-c579cb3ad76f"},{"title":"Boots, a Wizard Bear that Codes | Boot.dev","url":"https://boot.dev/blog/news/introducing-boots-ai-code-explainer"},{"title":"When Learning to Code Feels Like an RPG: My Boot.dev Review — Class Central","url":"https://www.classcentral.com/report/review-boot-dev/"},{"title":"Introducing Boots, the Artificially Intelligent Bear That Explains Code | Boot.dev","url":"https://blog.boot.dev/news/introducing-boots-ai-code-explainer/"},{"title":"Learn to Code | Boot.dev","url":"https://www.boot.dev/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about Boot.dev's Boots AI mentor and its Socratic method:\n\n## Boots: The Socratic AI Mentor\n\nBoot.dev's built-in AI mentor — Boots answers questions about the lesson you are on Socratically, with hints instead of solutions.\n\n### How It Works\n\nBoots has been instructed to use the Socratic method to help you learn, which means he'll ask you questions to help you learn rather than give you the answer. Boots is an AI chatbot (like ChatGPT) that has access to your lesson.\n\n### The Penalty Mechanism\n\nTo encourage independent problem-solving, Boot.dev has implemented an incentive system: Starting a conversation with Boots before you've completed a lesson costs 1 baked salmon (he's a hungry guy), or, if you don't have one, 50% of the XP for the lesson. However, chatting with Boots after you've completed a lesson is free, and encouraged for deepening your understanding.\n\n### Philosophy Behind the Design\n\nBoots is designed to not give you the answer, but instead use the Socratic method to help you figure it out yourself, and you're actually penalized (in game terms) for using him so you'll only use him when you truly need the help."],"durationSeconds":7.021207125000001,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JjFgKNkQTnQC1paBsXyqeD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SimConverse AI patient simulation nursing communication training how it works scoring\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SimConverse Utilizes AI to Improve Clinical Communication Skills Training | HealthySimulation.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.healthysimulation.com/simconverse-generative-ai-healthcare-simulation-communication-skills/\"},{\"title\":\"SimConverse | HealthySimulation.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.healthysimulation.com/simconverse-/\"},{\"title\":\"Students Master Patient Assessments with Simulated Preparation | Villanova University\",\"url\":\"https://www.villanova.edu/villanova/nursing/newsevents/archives/SimConverse.html\"},{\"title\":\"AI Use in Pharmacy Education: Service Evaluation of Using SimConverse for Simulation-Based Teaching – Active Learning at King's\",\"url\":\"https://blogs.kcl.ac.uk/activelearning/2026/05/18/ai-use-in-pharmacy-education-service-evaluation-of-using-simconverse-for-simulation-based-teaching/\"},{\"title\":\"Increase Clinical Training Capacity with SimConverse’s Large-Scale Communication Platform | HealthySimulation.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.healthysimulation.com/simconverse-communication-skills-ai-training/\"},{\"title\":\"Artificial Intelligence in Healthcare Simulation | HealthySimulation.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.healthysimulation.com/artificial-intelligence-healthcare-simulation/\"},{\"title\":\"Simconverse | Research\",\"url\":\"https://www.simconverse.com/research\"},{\"title\":\"Web-Based AI-Driven Virtual Patient Simulator Versus Actor-Based Simulation for Teaching Consultation Skills: Multicenter Randomized Crossover Study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12634008/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about SimConverse AI:\n\n## What It Is\n\nSimConverse has developed an online generative artificial intelligence (AI) platform to improve healthcare professionals' communication skills through virtual simulation experiences. SimConverse is an Australian-based company with a medical simulation platform that uses generative AI to play the role of any patient or healthcare colleague for healthcare communications training.\n\n## How It Works\n\nWith the ability to verbally communicate directly via conversational speech with SimConverse, healthcare learners can ask clinical questions and receive accurate simulated patient responses immediately. Using machine learning and Artificial Intelligence, SimConverse provides a multitude of simulated virtual patients complete with medical history, chief complaint, and physical examination findings.\n\nSimConverse was designed to operate within a simulated environment that is safe, repeatable, reflective, and customizable. The AI language model that SimConverse has developed is adaptable to any level of clinical learner and can portray any patient, colleague, or simulated participant role that a scenario requires.\n\n## Scoring and Feedback\n\nSimConverse supports faculty in all aspects of simulation: pre-work, scenario delivery, automated grading with quantitative and qualitative feedback, as well as facilitated self-reflection and debrief. Additionally, following each interaction, students receive detailed personalised feedback, along with access to assessment rubrics and conversation transcripts to support reflection and ongoing learning.\n\n## Effectiveness\n\nAn evaluation of downstream clinical performance with the SEGUE communication skills assessment framework showed nursing learners improved by 1.65 SD (p < 0.001).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e45f550-5a65-4305-802e-931b3b49c5e2","uuid":"4d8d4cca-1842-4f8a-bd7d-face4b5eb6a9","timestamp":"2026-08-11T02:33:32.313Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"SimConverse AI patient simul